🔄 Flow Logic (Step-by-Step)

1. Trigger
- The flow starts when a new email arrives (V3)

2. Data Initialization
- Initialize an array variable to store extracted items

3. Item Collection
- Loop through email content or attachment data  
- Append parsed values into an array 
  -  Yield an one-item, comma-separated array, ["aaa,\r\nbbb,\r\nccc,\r\naaa"]
  
4. Data Normalization : Our final goal is to split it to ["aaa","bbb","ccc"]
- Convert the array into raw text  
- Split raw text into a structured array using ","  
- Filter out empty or invalid entries using "trim()" function
  - trim() is used to remove white space or line breaks : \r\n

5. Deduplication
- Remove duplicate values to ensure clean and concise output, using union() function

6. Combine items from an array back into a single string, separated by a specified delimiter. Final data visualization purpose. 
- Join()
- This is because in the last step Adaptive Card, we can only put pure text into JSON text.


7. Presentation Formatting
- Join cleaned items into Adaptive Card–ready JSON text  
- Convert HTML content into plain text for consistent rendering

8. Output
- Post an Adaptive Card message into a Microsoft Teams chat or channel
